{%- comment -%}
  meta-tags.liquid  —  REVISED
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Drop-in replacement for snippets/meta-tags.liquid on the CURRENT live theme:
    gid://shopify/OnlineStoreTheme/145901649971
    "GS-style PDP + gallery/swatch fix Sep 24"
    role MAIN, 10649 bytes, updatedAt 2026-09-24T21:45:29Z

  REBASE NOTE. An earlier draft of this file was written against theme
  145734172723, which was MAIN when the audit started and has since been
  unpublished. Two things changed in the new theme and this version accounts
  for both:

    - The `sameAs` empty-string defect is FIXED. The old block emitted all six
      social settings unconditionally; the new one guards each with
      `!= blank`, assembles via `capture` + `remove_last: ','`, and only emits
      the property when the result is non-blank. Nothing to fix there. The new
      theme's own comment is also right that empty array entries were never a
      negative ranking signal — Google ignores them. Credit where due.
    - `config/settings_data.json` shows only two of the six links are set:
      Instagram and Facebook, both `celestelamourr`. So `sameAs` renders two
      URLs. That is a thin entity graph, not a broken one — the fix is to fill
      in the other profiles, not to change code.

  WHAT THIS VERSION CHANGES, AND WHY

  1. HOMEPAGE ENTITY MARKUP MOVED OUT to `brand-organization`.
     The live Organization node emits four properties — name, logo
     (conditional), sameAs (conditional), url. No @id, legalName, description,
     address, telephone, email, contactPoint or brand. Those are the values
     Google's Organization documentation lists as recommended, and every one of
     them already exists in your Shopify admin.
     Calibration, because this matters: Organization markup produces no rich
     result and does not guarantee a knowledge panel. Google's own docs say
     "there are no required properties." It is a cheap, high-value input to
     entity disambiguation — not a switch. Deploy it, but do not expect it to
     move anything on its own while 170 product pages declare a rival brand.

  2. PRODUCT `brand` BECOMES A REFERENCE, NOT `product.vendor`.
     This is the important one. The live line is:
         "brand": { "@type": "Brand", "name": {{ product.vendor | json }} }
     and `vendor` is `Gymshark` on 170 of 356 active products. That renders
     `"brand":{"@type":"Brand","name":"Gymshark"}` on 170 live, crawlable
     celestelamour.com URLs.
     Pointing at the single `#brand` node makes every product resolve to one
     entity. But understand what this is: a containment measure, not a fix. It
     stops the markup contradicting you while you do the real work in
     ../../google/worklist-competitor-products.md, which is deciding what those
     170 products are doing in the catalogue at all. Shipping this snippet and
     leaving the products would be papering over the problem — the URLs and
     titles still say Gymshark.

  3. OFFERS NO LONGER TRUNCATE. The live block emits one Offer per variant with
     `limit: 50`; products here carry up to 168 variants, so offers are being
     silently cut off. This emits a single Offer when every variant shares one
     price (the common case) and an AggregateOffer with a true offerCount when
     they differ.

  4. ADDED itemCondition, priceValidUntil, shippingDetails,
     hasMerchantReturnPolicy, a multi-image array, `category` and `@id`.
     Values come from the store's own published Shipping and Refund policies.

  5. META DESCRIPTION FALLS BACK to `shop.description`. The live block emits
     the tag only when `page_description` is non-blank. All 11 pages have no
     SEO metafields and `shop.description` is null, so no page renders a meta
     description at all. The fallback is worthless until that value is set —
     see ../../shopify/store-identity-values.md.

  6. og:image switched from `http:` to `https:`. The live block emits
     `content="http:{{ ... }}"` for og:image while using `https:` for
     og:image:secure_url. Minor, but it is a mixed-scheme reference.

  7. ADDED CollectionPage + ItemList markup, and breadcrumbs now route products
     through their collection so the trail is Home → Category → Product.

  UNCHANGED: title/OG/Twitter logic, and the `current_tags` handling with its
  comment about not piping a filter onto a translation argument — both correct.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign share_title = page_title
  assign share_kind = 'website'
  assign share_url = canonical_url
  assign share_summary = page_description | default: shop.description | default: shop.name
  assign share_media = blank

  case request.page_type
    when 'product'
      assign share_kind = 'product'
      if product.featured_media
        assign share_media = product.featured_media.preview_image
      endif
    when 'article'
      assign share_kind = 'article'
      if article.image
        assign share_media = article.image
      endif
    when 'collection'
      if collection.image
        assign share_media = collection.image
      endif
    when 'password'
      assign share_url = shop.url
  endcase

  if share_media == blank and settings.share_image
    assign share_media = settings.share_image
  endif
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  current_tags is joined into its own variable before it ever reaches a `t:`
  call. Piping a filter directly onto a translation argument
  (`t: tags: current_tags | join: ', '`) filters the translated string
  instead of the argument that was meant to feed it — exactly the kind of
  construct a strict Liquid parser flags on upload.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if current_tags -%}
  {%- assign tag_summary = current_tags | join: ', ' -%}
{%- endif -%}

<title>
  {{- page_title -}}
  {%- if current_tags %} | {{ 'general.meta.tags' | t: tags: tag_summary }}{% endif -%}
  {%- if current_page != 1 %} | {{ 'general.meta.page' | t: page: current_page }}{% endif -%}
  {%- unless page_title contains shop.name %} | {{ shop.name }}{% endunless -%}
</title>

{%- assign meta_description = page_description | default: shop.description -%}
{%- if meta_description != blank -%}
  <meta name="description" content="{{ meta_description | escape }}">
{%- endif -%}

<meta property="og:site_name" content="{{ shop.name }}">
<meta property="og:type" content="{{ share_kind }}">
<meta property="og:url" content="{{ share_url }}">
<meta property="og:title" content="{{ share_title | escape }}">
<meta property="og:description" content="{{ share_summary | escape }}">

{%- if share_media != blank -%}
  <meta property="og:image" content="https:{{ share_media | image_url: width: 1200 }}">
  <meta property="og:image:secure_url" content="https:{{ share_media | image_url: width: 1200 }}">
  <meta property="og:image:width" content="1200">
  <meta property="og:image:height" content="{{ 1200 | divided_by: share_media.aspect_ratio | round }}">
  <meta property="og:image:alt" content="{{ share_media.alt | escape }}">
{%- endif -%}

{%- if request.page_type == 'product' -%}
  <meta property="og:price:amount" content="{{ product.price | divided_by: 100.0 }}">
  <meta property="og:price:currency" content="{{ cart.currency.iso_code }}">
{%- endif -%}

<meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image">
<meta name="twitter:title" content="{{ share_title | escape }}">
<meta name="twitter:description" content="{{ share_summary | escape }}">

{%- comment -%} ---------- Structured data ---------- {%- endcomment -%}

{%- if request.page_type == 'index' -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    Organization + WebSite live in their own snippet now. Declared once, on the
    homepage only — Google expects a single Organization entity per site.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {% render 'brand-organization' %}
{%- endif -%}

{%- if request.page_type == 'product' -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign org_id = shop.url | append: '/#organization'
    assign brand_id = shop.url | append: '/#brand'
    assign return_id = shop.url | append: '/#returnpolicy'
    assign product_abs_url = shop.url | append: product.url

    assign rating_value = product.metafields.reviews.rating.value.rating
    assign rating_count = product.metafields.reviews.rating_count.value | plus: 0

    # A supplier SKU looks like `191288010:-1#Pink;191288664:28313#Xs`.
    # Treat anything containing a colon or a hash as not a retail identifier.
    assign raw_sku = product.selected_or_first_available_variant.sku
    assign sku_is_clean = true
    if raw_sku == blank
      assign sku_is_clean = false
    elsif raw_sku contains ':' or raw_sku contains '#'
      assign sku_is_clean = false
    endif

    assign price_valid_until = 'now' | date: '%Y' | plus: 1
    assign price_valid_until = price_valid_until | append: '-12-31'

    assign single_price = false
    if product.price_min == product.price_max
      assign single_price = true
    endif
  -%}
  <script type="application/ld+json">
    {
      "@context": "https://schema.org/",
      "@type": "Product",
      "@id": {{ product_abs_url | append: '#product' | json }},
      "name": {{ product.title | strip_html | json }},
      "url": {{ product_abs_url | json }},
      "description": {{ product.description | strip_html | strip_newlines | truncate: 5000 | json }},
      {%- if product.media.size > 0 -%}
      "image": [
        {%- for m in product.media limit: 6 -%}
          {{ m | image_url: width: 1920 | prepend: 'https:' | json }}{%- unless forloop.last -%},{%- endunless -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
      ],
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if sku_is_clean -%}
      "sku": {{ raw_sku | json }},
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if product.type != blank -%}
      "category": {{ product.type | json }},
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- comment -%}
        See note 2 in the header. This points at the one brand node declared on
        the homepage instead of echoing `product.vendor`, which is `Gymshark`
        on 170 of 356 active products. Containment, not a cure — fix the
        catalogue.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      "brand": { "@id": {{ brand_id | json }} },

      {%- comment -%}
        AGGREGATERATING — READ BEFORE ENABLING.

        This reads `product.metafields.reviews.rating`, the Shopify-native
        namespace, and deliberately does NOT read `judgeme.*`.

        Current state, verified 2026-09-24: across the first 50 active
        products, NONE carries a `reviews.rating` metafield, and every
        `judgeme.badge` reads `data-average-rating='0.00'
        data-number-of-reviews='0'`. So this block does not fire today and no
        rating markup is being emitted. Good.

        The reason for the guard is what sits behind it. Judge.me reports 142
        reviews store-wide at 4.69, and DRAFT product 7830848110643 carries a
        badge advertising 100 reviews at 4.60 whose bodies read, verbatim:
          "DEMO / TEST REVIEW — NOT FOR PUBLICATION. Layout test scenario 100…"
        under reviewer names like "DEMO S.B.", all verified_buyer: false.

        That is a landmine, not a live violation: it fires the moment those
        drafts are published, or if Judge.me's own rich-snippet feature is
        switched on independently of the theme (Judge.me → Settings → SEO).

        Before wiring any review app in here: delete the DEMO rows, confirm the
        remaining count is real, and confirm the reviews are visible on the
        page — Google requires the marked-up rating to be present in visible
        content.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if rating_value != blank and rating_count > 0 -%}
      "aggregateRating": {
        "@type": "AggregateRating",
        "ratingValue": {{ rating_value | json }},
        "bestRating": 5,
        "worstRating": 1,
        "reviewCount": {{ rating_count }}
      },
      {%- endif -%}

      "offers": {
        {%- if single_price -%}
        "@type": "Offer",
        "price": {{ product.price_min | divided_by: 100.0 }},
        {%- else -%}
        "@type": "AggregateOffer",
        "lowPrice": {{ product.price_min | divided_by: 100.0 }},
        "highPrice": {{ product.price_max | divided_by: 100.0 }},
        "offerCount": {{ product.variants.size }},
        {%- endif -%}
        "priceCurrency": {{ cart.currency.iso_code | json }},
        "priceValidUntil": {{ price_valid_until | json }},
        "itemCondition": "https://schema.org/NewCondition",
        "availability": {% if product.available %}"https://schema.org/InStock"{% else %}"https://schema.org/OutOfStock"{% endif %},
        "url": {{ product_abs_url | json }},
        "seller": { "@id": {{ org_id | json }} },
        "hasMerchantReturnPolicy": { "@id": {{ return_id | json }} },

        {%- comment -%}
          Shipping figures come from the published Shipping policy: 1–3
          business days handling, Standard 3–5 business days at $7.99, free
          Standard at $75+. If the policy changes, change this too — shipping
          markup that contradicts the policy page is worse than none, because
          Google cross-checks it and can suppress the annotation domain-wide.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        "shippingDetails": {
          "@type": "OfferShippingDetails",
          "shippingRate": {
            "@type": "MonetaryAmount",
            "value": 7.99,
            "currency": "USD"
          },
          "shippingDestination": {
            "@type": "DefinedRegion",
            "addressCountry": "US"
          },
          "deliveryTime": {
            "@type": "ShippingDeliveryTime",
            "handlingTime": {
              "@type": "QuantitativeValue",
              "minValue": 1,
              "maxValue": 3,
              "unitCode": "DAY"
            },
            "transitTime": {
              "@type": "QuantitativeValue",
              "minValue": 3,
              "maxValue": 5,
              "unitCode": "DAY"
            }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  </script>
{%- endif -%}

{%- if request.page_type == 'article' -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    AUTHOR — this is currently emitting nonsense.

    `article.author` on the live blog resolves to `5K20RB-1R` on three of the
    five published articles, and to `PageFly` on another. `5K20RB-1R` is the
    store's myshopify subdomain in capitals. So the live markup declares a
    schema.org **Person named "5K20RB-1R"** authoring content for this brand.

    The guard below falls back to the organization when the stored author is
    obviously not a person — the myshopify handle, or an app name. That is a
    patch over bad data, not a fix: set real authors in Online Store → Blog
    posts → [article] → Author. See ../../google/worklist-blog-cleanup.md.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign author_raw = article.author | strip
    assign author_upper = author_raw | upcase
    assign shop_handle_upper = shop.permanent_domain | split: '.' | first | upcase
    assign author_is_person = true
    if author_raw == blank
      assign author_is_person = false
    elsif author_upper == shop_handle_upper
      assign author_is_person = false
    elsif author_upper == 'PAGEFLY'
      assign author_is_person = false
    endif
  -%}
  <script type="application/ld+json">
    {
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "Article",
      "@id": {{ shop.url | append: article.url | append: '#article' | json }},
      "headline": {{ article.title | json }},
      "articleBody": {{ article.content | strip_html | json }},
      {% if article.image -%}
        "image": [{{ article.image | image_url: width: 1920 | prepend: "https:" | json }}],
      {%- endif %}
      "datePublished": {{ article.published_at | date: '%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ' | json }},
      "dateModified": {{ article.updated_at | default: article.published_at | date: '%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ' | json }},
      {%- if author_is_person -%}
      "author": { "@type": "Person", "name": {{ author_raw | json }} },
      {%- else -%}
      "author": { "@id": {{ shop.url | append: '/#organization' | json }} },
      {%- endif -%}
      "publisher": { "@id": {{ shop.url | append: '/#organization' | json }} },
      "isPartOf": { "@id": {{ shop.url | append: '/#website' | json }} },
      "mainEntityOfPage": { "@type": "WebPage", "@id": {{ shop.url | append: article.url | json }} }
    }
  </script>
{%- endif -%}

{%- if request.page_type == 'collection' -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    NEW. Collection pages previously emitted only a BreadcrumbList. A
    CollectionPage with an ItemList gives Google an explicit, named,
    navigational entity per category — raw material for sitelinks.

    Worth being straight about the limits: Google's sitelinks documentation
    names page titles and headings, a logical site structure with important
    pages linked from relevant pages, and concise internal anchor text. It does
    not name structured data. This markup helps Google understand the page; it
    is the navigation and internal-linking work in
    ../../google/worklist-collections-sitelinks.md that actually produces
    sitelinks. Ship both, expect the results from that one.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <script type="application/ld+json">
    {
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "CollectionPage",
      "@id": {{ shop.url | append: collection.url | append: '#collection' | json }},
      "url": {{ shop.url | append: collection.url | json }},
      "name": {{ collection.title | json }},
      {%- if collection.description != blank -%}
      "description": {{ collection.description | strip_html | strip_newlines | truncate: 500 | json }},
      {%- endif -%}
      "isPartOf": { "@id": {{ shop.url | append: '/#website' | json }} },
      "about": { "@id": {{ shop.url | append: '/#brand' | json }} },
      "mainEntity": {
        "@type": "ItemList",
        "numberOfItems": {{ collection.products_count }},
        "itemListElement": [
          {%- for p in collection.products limit: 12 -%}
          {
            "@type": "ListItem",
            "position": {{ forloop.index }},
            "url": {{ shop.url | append: p.url | json }},
            "name": {{ p.title | strip_html | json }}
          }{%- unless forloop.last -%},{%- endunless -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
        ]
      }
    }
  </script>
{%- endif -%}

{%- if request.page_type == 'product' or request.page_type == 'collection' or request.page_type == 'article' -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign crumb_collection = blank
    if request.page_type == 'product'
      assign crumb_collection = product.metafields.custom.category_collection.value
      if crumb_collection == blank
        assign crumb_collection = collection
      endif
      if crumb_collection == blank
        assign crumb_collection = product.collections.first
      endif
    endif
  -%}
  <script type="application/ld+json">
    {
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
      "itemListElement": [
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          "position": 1,
          "name": {{ 'general.breadcrumbs.home' | t | json }},
          "item": {{ shop.url | json }}
        }
        {%- if request.page_type == 'product' -%}
          {%- if crumb_collection != blank -%},
          {
            "@type": "ListItem",
            "position": 2,
            "name": {{ crumb_collection.title | json }},
            "item": {{ shop.url | append: crumb_collection.url | json }}
          },
          {
            "@type": "ListItem",
            "position": 3,
            "name": {{ product.title | json }},
            "item": {{ shop.url | append: product.url | json }}
          }
          {%- else -%},
          {
            "@type": "ListItem",
            "position": 2,
            "name": {{ product.title | json }},
            "item": {{ shop.url | append: product.url | json }}
          }
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- elsif request.page_type == 'collection' -%},
          {
            "@type": "ListItem",
            "position": 2,
            "name": {{ collection.title | json }},
            "item": {{ shop.url | append: collection.url | json }}
          }
        {%- elsif request.page_type == 'article' -%},
          {
            "@type": "ListItem",
            "position": 2,
            "name": {{ blog.title | json }},
            "item": {{ shop.url | append: blog.url | json }}
          },
          {
            "@type": "ListItem",
            "position": 3,
            "name": {{ article.title | json }},
            "item": {{ shop.url | append: article.url | json }}
          }
        {%- endif -%}
      ]
    }
  </script>
{%- endif -%}
